Mastering Monitoring with CloudWatch + SNS 📬
Topic: Smart Monitoring & Alerting with Amazon CloudWatch + SNS

Today’s focus in my AWSChallenge: Learning how to monitor cloud infrastructure and set up real-time alerts using CloudWatch + SNS (Simple Notification Service). These tools form the backbone of any DevOps monitoring and incident response system. 🔧📊

🔍 What is Amazon CloudWatch?
CloudWatch is AWS’s observability service used for:

Monitoring EC2, Lambda, RDS, ALB, EBS, and more

Setting alarms on metrics like CPU, memory, disk, network

Collecting and visualizing logs and custom metrics

Automating actions (like stopping instances)

📬 What is Amazon SNS?
SNS is a pub/sub messaging service used to send:

Emails 📧

SMS 📲

HTTP/HTTPS webhook notifications

Lambda triggers

ChatOps integration (Slack, Teams, etc.)

🔁 Real-World Use Case Setup:
✅ Created CloudWatch Alarm

Triggered when EC2 CPU > 70%

✅ Integrated with SNS

Configured email alert for instant notification

✅ Bonus:

Used CloudWatch Logs to monitor app logs

Set up log-based metrics to trigger alerts on error keywords

⚙️ Architecture Flow:
1️⃣ AWS Resource (e.g., EC2, Lambda, RDS)
⬇️
2️⃣ CloudWatch monitors & creates alarm
⬇️
3️⃣ Alarm triggers SNS topic
⬇️
4️⃣ SNS sends alert (email, SMS, webhook, Lambda)

💡 DevOps Use Cases:
Alerting on high CPU, memory, disk

Get notified when an instance is stopped or failed

Alert on app log anomalies (error, exception, timeout)

Chain actions: alert + auto scale or restart instance

Compliance monitoring & audit triggers

🚀 Why It Matters:
With CloudWatch + SNS, you’re not just monitoring—you’re automating awareness.
No more manually checking dashboards. Be the first to know when something breaks.
